{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0458","billNumberShort":"H.B. 458","billNumberLong":"HB0458","fileNumber":"2026FL0114","shortTitle":"Preterm Birth Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"SHEPHL","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shepherd, Lisa","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCCAYD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McCay, Daniel","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses preterm birth policies.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>requires facilities that provide birthing services to:<hr><ltbullet1>develop and publish policies regarding preterm birth;<hr><ltbullet1>inform parents about the facility's capability to provide lifesaving care for a premature infant; and<hr><ltbullet1>report to the Department of Health and Human Services regarding preterm births;<hr><ltbullet>requires a provider to consult with a neonatologist in certain circumstances relating to risk of preterm delivery;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits the denial of lifesaving care to an infant based solely on the gestational age of the infant;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Department of Health and Human Services to produce an annual report regarding preterm birth in the state;<hr><ltbullet>requires prenatal health care providers to discuss certain things with a pregnant patient before approximately 20 weeks gestation;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the rights of a patient during preterm birth; and<hr><ltbullet>defines terms.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kami Orton","fiscalAnalyst":"Kevin Edminster","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"YEAYIFXAQW","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-02 11:46:00.060","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":"